<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes continue in Bangui among government forces, former Séléka rebels, Anti-balaka militias, Russian Wagner troops and Africa Corps, while the United Nations warns against a premature peacekeeper withdrawal. Chad arrested four suspects after an attack in Miski, and CAR officials denied that their forces crossed the Chad border during a raid. Three former hostages were released and greeted by President Touadéra on their return to Bangui. The conflict caused 246 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxPWFoyR0J1TXZlcHpTR0RmSW9rN2V1RU54cEVDU1BvUmZLcjRpNGFSUXBhNktSRXVOTllkOW54RmV5YUhxRlZjamt3S1dmVklNbXNiQ0E4SHNBWk5UU0RJT0c5Rmp6N3hvRjZkdklCMW9UR3h6YVZQZU9MNnlCTEV6TG9ZRUdoSnVCTzJueEdRQ3ZjaWdXZk8tRkpkNFZGYkJmX2RQdlNtcFBzeWNzWnZZajNPVzItcmcyVXRDWVpmSQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxORGtfcFhSaXlZOW01WjJhTEVWcTBQSlN4OTIxb2J3SmxmQ0prZ1dkTEpVckFGY2hQSlgyZzBjTl9RRXlOZ1JWdU5BSUhIZ2pTYmhCQW5WU0ZnUWNUdUlWSVRXajJ1dVRFMFhUN2Zkai1vMGxqS29mUDNTaHVud0FQNVJvb0NVcW5rNmFUVzNod3N2NTd1VkZWUGZadW9oVTVPb1NFQmsxWlhfU2RSWTVPN2dlUnlOd2ItSGRfdHZ3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxQS2NWMWktckdtQV8zeFdpZk8yV1J0RlNVSFQ1Y2lfc0tRc3NlYWdvR1Fsb3V1bjllX2xsdkJkaXZ2eTlfaWNsSXZndDRNc2ZSRGlGWWVvTVUyV2IzS2tIemxsUzEtTG1pZ3oyTG1iZHBGeHE4elNmQkZKRnN1YXhPRkhrQnZOZ2RPakJ3c3hvN21HOXFMOTZwalRNRjVYNFE3MmFnZmFtYXYyZ29qQ3MxU1VMa1pXd2Jx?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMie0FVX3lxTE03c01BNjE5b3piRFdpV09yWFloQmhlLXV5el9tRjREZUgwbjdOZW1WWkw5MUh6OUtHSmVGNGpQVlFGdnNrX1VFcXVMTngzdWhqcFM4Q1dfWHBGSWw1